The memory of a response by its length (aZ, 22.11.2026), the length a hint to zstd
and not a promise. ZSTD_initCStream(cstream, level) took the window of the level
whatever the response, and the context had the memory of it: at level 3 (libzstd
1.5.5 and 1.5.7) 3577 KiB a response. Now a response of a known length has that
length given to zstd by ZSTD_c_srcSizeHint, and zstd sizes its window and tables to
it (libzstd 1.5.5: 1273 KiB for a response of 100 KB, 325 KiB for one of 10 KB), and
one without a length has the window capped at 2^19 (2041 KiB; 512 KiB in place of
2 MiB). The Content-Length is taken in the header filter before
ngx_http_clear_content_length() clears it, as HanadaLee 9113bbb and myguard-labs do.
Not ZSTD_CCtx_setPledgedSrcSize(), which this patch had first (1068 KiB for 100 KB):
zstd fails a stream whose input is not of the pledged length ("Src size is
incorrect"), and the Content-Length of a response is not always that of its body: a
body filter of Lua that does not clear it, a Content-Length of content_by_lua or of
more_set_headers. gzip and brotli size their windows by the same length and compress
such a body whole, and so does zstd with the hint (the review of 22.11.2026: 12
responses of 12 cut with the pledge, none with the hint, over HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2 and
HTTP/3). No hint above 8 MB: a client of the "zstd" content coding takes a window of
up to 8 MB (RFC 9659), and the levels 20 to 22 have larger ones for a longer
response. With a dictionary (zstd_dict_file, not used) the module as it is. A libzstd
that does not take the hint (before 1.4.4): the window by the length.
Applied by post-patch in WRKSRC_zstd after extra-patch-zstd-config, -p0.

